    "body": "The new Rust public-equation solver adds dependency scheduling and rollback invalidation to partial linear/quadratic extraction. It consumes System, public semantic role indices and fixed limits; no labels/signs/point list/witness enter the query. Native PCC-20261116-fb7763 is unsigned/unverified. [pcc:unverified]\n\nOn all 13 fixed Fp101/a17/q3/k8 arity2 public targets, indexed worklist returns original-checked roots and independent raw-index/group replay. Original worklist returns 13 Unsupported outcomes; original sweep records 13 cumulative modeled-reservation caps; indexed sweep returns 5 roots and 8 such caps. All 52 outcomes/decision traces remain in the complete raw archive, with no raised-limit retry. Both scheduling arms on each representation of the distinct actual-field q1/k2/two-column fixture return the same root/decision trace and replay +column(1,0)+column(2,0). This is not the original huge q213156431 base or a six-member discovery claim. [pcc:unverified]\n\nReverse 64 chain records 4160 versus 191 equation revisions while BOTH still scan 4160 cached statuses. These are partial diagnostics, not timing, total normalized work, live RAM, a speed comparison or an exponent result. Derived auxiliaries never branch; coupled/high-degree residuals may return Unsupported. Complete cold setup/parser/allocation/check/index/group replay accounting remains open. No paid job, campaign, full actual-base search or broad root-library rerun was run. [pcc:unverified]\n\nValidation: focused release library controls, fmt and strict all-target Clippy pass locally. The first unit attempt failed from a wrong fixture binding; exact failed source/log remain. Source-bound separate binary/pre-call qualifier covers 55 composite inputs and all six compiled-in pins; no native source changed after qualification. Full raw tree is one prescribed 10,992-byte archive, with original hashes for 1,782,635-byte controls.json and both actual systems. Report PCC-20261116-fd44ad pins the inspected final two-page PDF, Markdown/TeX, editable pipeline and recorded-revision chart; first overfull layout retained. All standing is unsigned/unverified. [pcc:unverified]\n\nPredecessor #4397 is terminal: externally merged 20:16:38Z into main as cd6194a7/head9dff. Closure PCC-20261116-869d20, episode E-9ad1262e3c79 and outcome O-ffce2552fe60 cover publication-to-merge only. Postmerge 41-check snapshot does not establish all-green-at-merge. Study/claim file blobs survive; canonical upstream integration omitted 38 prior published lane registrations and some journal blocks. Those discrepancies remain explicit; no old record was repaired, re-registered or re-chained. Its checker was disabled. [pcc:unverified]\n\nThis follow-up starts from canonical main and appends ONLY its new unpublished claim bodies, with backed-up unpublished event/journal suffix and complete transfer receipt. Full local ledger gate has 125 inherited missing claim_type errors, identical on exact untouched main and this working tree; chain-only/prefix/new-schema checks have zero errors. No historical schema edit, policy/exemption, signer/verifier, credential workaround or CI bypass is included. New actual-head hosted gate/size/artifacts and reviews remain required; auto-merge is a request, not a gate waiver. [pcc:unverified]\n\nEvidence: research/curve25519_torus_native_20261115/worklist-solver-v1/{PROTOCOL.md,FROZEN.md,REPRODUCE.md,PUBLISHING.md,NEXT.md}, reports/worklist-solver-v1/REPORT.md and pr-closure-4397-20261116/. Canonical cost/exponent/benchmark graphs stay unchanged because no admitted performance datum was added. Next is complete cold accounting and independent cached-evaluator/semantic-boundary checks before a separately admitted matched growing-family solver comparison. Original route criteria remain unchanged. [pcc:unverified]\n\nInput retention scope: both actual-field Systems are exported in the raw archive. Toy Systems are reconstructed from the frozen compiler/spec/retained public targets and role indices; v1 does not separately serialize/seal all26 toy input Systems. The future cold comparison must freeze those exact input exports before execution. [pcc:unverified]\n",
